# dsv41: KV-sharded decode exchanges on the family's RDMA ring. 0015's decode ran its exchanges as NCCL collectives on
# the main stream (fetch: two all-gathers of R x 512 rows a compressed layer; owner: a query all-gather plus an
# exchange), where the replicated engine rides the GPU-driven RDMA ring inside its graphs. Now, with the ring
# configured (TF_RDMA_DEVICES; the recipe's RDMA=1), each decode exchange rides it, sized to the rows that really cross
# (shard_ring.zig: explicit row lists, the same on both ranks, uploaded each round to one fixed block so captured
# graphs stay valid; stage and collect kernels in dsv41_shard.cu), owner decode's own-head pass and early query stage
# run on a side stream of their own (TF_DS_KV_SHARD_OVERLAP), and TF_DS_KV_SHARD_DECODE=auto chooses fetch or owner each
# round from a cost model (shard_ring.decide, a pure function of what both ranks hold). Shard phase clocks and
# counters (ring rounds, auto's choices, rows sent) for profiles (tf-dsv41-lanes); a ring transfer out of its fixed
# order or rows refuses on both ranks and ends the pair (round.pair_ending, 0020). The parts' stats behind /health
# are rebuilt at most every 250 ms (they were rebuilt every engine-loop pass).
# Switches (both ranks, agreed unless noted): TF_DS_KV_SHARD_RING 1 (0: NCCL), TF_DS_KV_SHARD_DECODE fetch, owner or
# auto, TF_DS_KV_SHARD_COST (auto's nine costs, ns), TF_DS_KV_SHARD_OVERLAP on (per rank, not agreed). All inert
# without TF_DS_KV_SHARD=1.
# Measured on the pair: with the ring and the cached stats a sharded decode round (a row fetch every round) costs ~1-4 %
# against the base at 1 to 8 streams (bench.py, 3 reps; round 2's NCCL fetch cost 10.6-12.3 %); the daily config
# (KV_SHARD=1, pool 2,101,248, SPILL_GIB=64; engine 569bdd1, before the rebase onto 0008) exact.py 39/39 identical, and
# identical again on the rebased engine (this series' tip, with the display-reserve patch beside it, pool 5,218,304).
# Builds on 0018 and 0020. By Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo). Apache-2.0.
